From df7cd7a758673511a198242aa0175c7b292d4a33 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Claude (fill agent)" <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 22:36:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 05/12] NDNormalForm: a work tape's replay on tape 1, its exit
 invariant and clear

One block of a work
tape's replay (read, check against the decoded claim, rewrite with the new
content, move two cells per simulated move, skipping the move after the
end-flagged record), the read of one record by a work-tape instance, the block
representation of a replayed work tape on tape 1 with its decode, write and
support lemmas, the work-tape replay over a stream of records with the exit
invariant (tape 1 blank outside a nonempty contiguous nonblank region holding
its head), and the region read as the clear's blank-delimited word. The two
run lemmas now share the split of a stream's checks at its first record, the
flags of its tail, and the control's agreement with the virtual run.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
